00:29:01.440 --> 00:29:03.260
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Meron pong ganon. Meron pong ganon.

00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:22.305
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Now, let's go to the fact that several corporations did not declare any dividends, no? You are aware naman po, Atty. Del Rosario, at kasi abogado naman po kayo at matagal na po kayo sa SEC, That the power of a corporation to declare dividends is under section 42 of our revised corporation code.

00:29:22.305 --> 00:29:23.630
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:29:24.130 --> 00:29:24.770
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: And

00:29:24.770 --> 00:29:52.270
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: you confirm that under section 42 of the revised corporation code, it states that, and I quote, the board of directors of a stock corporation may declare dividends out of unrestricted retained earnings which shall be payable in cash, property, or in stock to all stockholders on the basis of the outstanding stock held by them. Naka-flash po siya but you can confirm po if tama yung...

00:29:52.270 --> 00:29:52.640
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:29:52.640 --> 00:29:59.910
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Section 42. Okay. Now you confirm that under Section 42 of the Revised Corporation Code with respect to the...

00:30:05.280 --> 00:30:06.870
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Tama po ba?

00:30:06.870 --> 00:30:08.160
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:30:20.280 --> 00:30:22.220
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:30:29.980 --> 00:30:32.960
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Unrestricted retained earnings. Tama po ba ang pagkaintindi ko sa batas?

00:30:32.960 --> 00:30:33.370
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:30:33.370 --> 00:30:41.240
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Now you are also aware, however, na may paragraph 2 itong section 42 ng revised corporation code. Tama po ba?

00:30:41.240 --> 00:30:42.430
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:30:42.430 --> 00:30:48.200
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: And dito po nakalagay yung prohibition on retaining surplus profits. Tama po ba?

00:30:48.200 --> 00:30:48.810
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:30:48.810 --> 00:31:01.900
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: And specifically it states, the prohibition is only that a stock corporation are prohibited from retaining surplus profits. in excess of 100% of their paid-in capital. Tama po ba?

00:31:01.900 --> 00:31:03.520
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:31:03.520 --> 00:31:07.300
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Okay, may question. Ito po yung paid-in capital.

00:31:08.940 --> 00:31:17.620
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: This is the total amount of cash or property actually contributed by shareholders in relation to the subscribed shares. Tama po ba?

00:31:17.620 --> 00:31:18.610
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:31:18.610 --> 00:31:32.870
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: So sa madaling salita po, ito yung mga amount of shares ng isang kumpanya na payad na talaga ng shareholders whether it be by property or whether it be by cash or other. Other allowable considerations for the purchase of shares. Tama?

00:31:32.870 --> 00:31:33.980
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Opo. Tama po.

00:31:33.980 --> 00:31:43.800
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Kasi pwede naman po para maintindihan po natin na mag-subscribe ng shares sa kumpanya at hindi mo bayaran yung buong subscription. Tama po ba?

