Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Maari po yan.

00:31:44.880 --> 00:31:51.350
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Kaya may distinction po sa summary na pre-prepare nyo, amount subscribed at amount paid up. Tama?

00:31:51.350 --> 00:31:52.430
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:31:52.430 --> 00:32:01.935
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Now let's go back under section 42. What is prohibited is not the fact That a corporation does not issue any dividends. Tama po ba?

00:32:01.935 --> 00:32:03.560
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Pakiulit po.

00:32:03.560 --> 00:32:18.960
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Sorry. I'll do it slowly. Under Section 42, hindi naman prohibited ang hindi pag-declare ng dividendo. Tama po? Dahil sa word na may. What is prohibited is retaining surplus profits in excess by 100% of payment capital.

00:32:18.960 --> 00:32:19.970
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:32:19.970 --> 00:32:24.970
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: So kapag walang dineklara, hindi naman po illegal yung ginagawa ng mga korporasyon. Tama po ba?

00:32:24.970 --> 00:32:26.080
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Hindi naman po.

00:32:26.080 --> 00:32:46.100
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Okay. Pero kahit na, Under the prohibition on paragraph 42, you agree naman po, Atty. Del Rosario, na may exceptions kung saan pwede po tayong mag-withheld ng declaration of dividendo kahit na nag-exceed na yung surplus profits mo sa paid-in capital. Tama po ba?

00:32:46.260 --> 00:32:47.920
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Meron pong tatlong exception under

00:32:47.920 --> 00:33:02.800
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: section 42. At ito yung mga exception, just please confirm. A. When justified by definite expansion projects or programs approved by the Board of Directors. Tama po ba? Yan po yung una. Ito yung sa mga abogado tinatawag po

00:33:02.800 --> 00:33:05.790
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: natin na approved expansions for brevity. Tama po?

00:33:05.790 --> 00:33:06.650
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:33:06.650 --> 00:33:24.780
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Yung pangalawang exception naman po, when the corporation is prohibited under any loan agreement with financial institution or creditors, whether local or foreign, from declaring dividends without their consent and such consent has not yet been secured. Pwede din po, tama?

00:33:24.780 --> 00:33:25.460
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Apo.

00:33:25.460 --> 00:33:29.610
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Ito yung mga tinatawag natin na abogado na loan restrictions. Tama po ba?

00:33:29.610 --> 00:33:30.400
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:33:30.400 --> 00:33:47.340
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Now, yung pangatlo, when it can be clearly shown that such retention is necessary under special circumstances obtaining in the corporation, such as when there is a need for a special reserve for probable contingencies. Tama po ba?

00:33:47.340 --> 00:33:48.280
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Yan po yung pangatlo.

00:33:48.280 --> 00:33:51.900
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Ito yung tinatawag natin na special circumstances. Tama po ba?

00:33:51.900 --> 00:33:52.650
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:33:52.650 --> 00:33:58.765
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: At kasali dito, Ang yung mga kaso, halimbawa yung kumpanya, may litigation, tama po ba?

00:33:58.765 --> 00:34:00.230
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Tama po.

00:34:00.230 --> 00:34:12.555
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Okay. And you confirm, sir, na kapag ginagawa ito ng corporation, meaning invoking those three exceptions, dapat nire-report ito sa audited financial statement?

00:34:12.555 --> 00:34:13.890
Atty. Gerardo F. del Rosario: Dapat po.

00:34:13.890 --> 00:34:20.340
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Okay. Pero you confirm, sir, in the summary that you prepared, ang nilagay nyo lang, no dividends declared.

